$\frac{N_0}{N_1} = \frac{pQ_0+R_0}{pQ_1+R_1} \approx \frac{Q_0}{Q_1}$, with error $\frac{|R_0Q_1-R_1Q_0|}{N_1Q_1} \sim 2^{999}/2^{1776} = 2^{-777}$. Since $Q_1 \sim 2^{666}$, this error is far below $1/Q_1^2$, so $Q_0/Q_1$ appears as a **convergent of the continued fraction** of $N_0/N_1$. Once we recover $Q_0$, we get $p = \lfloor N_0/Q_0 \rfloor$ exactly (since $R_0 < Q_0$).

